  (text "Power subsystem -- USB-C 5V in, single 3.3V rail (pilink-7el.2)\nRP2350B's internal switched regulator makes its own 1.1V core voltage\nfrom this 3.3V rail (same pattern as stock Pico boards) -- no separate\n1.1V regulator on this sheet. +5V arrives from the USB-C sheet\n(pilink-7el.7); PWR_FLAG marks it as externally driven for ERC." (at 60.96 30.48 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 05f9001f-68b4-41c9-b633-340747c14553)
  )

  (text "U1: AMS1117-3.3, SOT-223, 800mA LDO (Advanced Monolithic Systems' own\ndatasheet rates it 800mA max output / 15V max input -- some vendors market\nAMS1117 clones as \"1A\", but that's not what the datasheet says). JLCPCB\nBasic part C6186 / LCSC C6186, stock in the hundreds of thousands of units\n(checked 2026-11-14). Pin-compatible (same SOT-223 pinout: 1=GND,\n2=VOUT/tab, 3=VIN) with the NCP1117-3.3 used in Raspberry Pi's own\nofficial RP2350B minimal reference design (arturo182/rp2350_minimal_kicad\nmirror of RP-006442-DD-2, RP2350_80QFN_minimal.kicad_sch) -- but NOT a\nfunctional/electrical equivalent: AMS1117 is rated 15V in / 800mA out vs\nNCP1117's 20V in / ~1A out, and their output-cap stability requirements\ndiffer (see decoupling note below). This design only needs 5V->3.3V at\nmodest current -- rough budget: RP2350B tens of mA, ESP32-WROOM-32U ~80mA\naverage (Espressif spec wants a supply capable of 500mA to cover Wi-Fi TX\nbursts), small ST7789V-class display ~50-100mA incl. backlight -- so\nAMS1117's 800mA rating keeps reasonable margin even under a worst-case\nsimultaneous peak; re-check once real current draws are measured." (at 60.96 46.99 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 7e9033c0-519c-4359-a2c3-9f2f753fbe3f)
  )

  (text "Decoupling: C1 10uF bulk on the regulator input (AMS1117 datasheet gives\nno input-cap minimum; matches the reference design's input cap C1). C2\n22uF on the output, per Advanced Monolithic Systems' real AMS1117\ndatasheet (see Datasheet link above): \"22uF solid tantalum on the output\nwill ensure stability for all operating conditions.\" NOT reusing the\nreference design's 10uF, which is sized for the different NCP1117 part\n(see note above). Using 22uF ceramic (0805) for cost/size; datasheet\nwants tantalum for ESR/stability, so verify at bring-up. C3 100nF local\nceramic at the 3V3 point-of-load is standard LDO-output practice, not a\nguide-mandated value -- RP-008280-DS-2 Rel. 3 Sec. 2.2.1 only covers\nRP2350B's own pins, which live on pilink-7el.3." (at 60.96 160.02 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 54487828-8fea-454b-a628-566a5c551201)
  )

  (text "Out of scope for this sheet (lives on the RP2350B + Memory sheet,\npilink-7el.3): RP2350B's ~11 per-pin 100nF VDD3V3/IOVDD decouplers, the\nVREG_LX/VREG_AVDD inductor+caps for its internal 3.3V->1.1V core\nregulator, and the 10uF bulk cap (C19 in the reference design) on +3V3\nnear the RP2350 -- this project splits what Raspberry Pi's single-sheet\nreference design combines, across this sheet and the RP2350B+memory one." (at 60.96 185.42 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 4f509b76-bf21-47f2-b154-7483f0eb276e)
  )
)
